+From 54bc0f02149d9704c00f23e311473307c6b044cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Fabio Paracchini <fparacchini@alteanet.it>
+Date: Tue, 31 Mar 2026 23:51:20 +0200
+Subject: [PATCH 13/19] feat: log OIDC claims on both success and failed login
+ in AccessLogMiddleware
+MIME-Version: 1.0
+Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
+Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit
+
+On success the oauth_id_token cookie is already extracted from the
+response Set-Cookie headers (patch 0023).
+
+For failures (domain restriction, role mismatch, signup disabled, …)
+the cookie is never set.  The token exchange with the IdP may still have
+succeeded, so the id_token containing the user's identity is available
+inside oauth.py but invisible to the middleware.
+
+Fix (two-file, minimal coupling):
+- oauth.py: after a successful authorize_access_token(), store
+  token['id_token'] in request.state.oidc_raw_id_token (4 lines).
+  This runs unconditionally before any validation that may raise 403/400.
+- AccessLogMiddleware: when the response-cookie path returns nothing
+  (failure case), fall back to request.state.oidc_raw_id_token and
+  decode it with the existing _decode_id_token_claims() helper.
+
+Coverage after fix:
+  Success (307):  oidc_sub=<sub>  mfa=pwd   (from response Set-Cookie)
+  Failure (4xx):  oidc_sub=<sub>  mfa=pwd   (from request.state)
+  Token exch err: oidc_sub=-  mfa=-          (no id_token available)
+
+Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
