+Subject: [PATCH 14/19] feat: log full OIDC token claims in AUTH_OIDC_LOGIN
+ access log line
+
+Add a 'claims=' JSON field to the ACCESS log line for AUTH_OIDC_LOGIN
+events (success and failure) so that claim mapping issues (wrong role
+claim name, missing email, unexpected groups, etc.) are immediately
+visible without requiring DEBUG log level.
+
+Changes in access_log.py:
+- import json (module-level)
+- _REDACTED_CLAIMS: frozenset of opaque internal claims excluded from
+  the dump (at_hash, c_hash, nonce, jti) to reduce noise and avoid
+  triggering WAF/DLP rules on opaque values
+- _decode_full_id_token(raw): new helper that returns the full decoded
+  payload dict minus redacted claims; returns None on error
+- dispatch(): tracks oidc_raw_id_token (from response Set-Cookie on
+  success, from request.state on failure); appends
+  'claims=<json>' to the log line only for AUTH_OIDC_LOGIN events
+
+Example log line (success):
+  WARNING | ... | action=AUTH_OIDC_LOGIN | outcome=redirect | nis2=Y |
+  ... | claims={"sub":"mario@co.it","email":"mario@co.it",
+  "amr":["pwd"],"roles":["user"],"groups":["all"]}
+
+Example log line (failure - role mismatch):
+  WARNING | ... | action=AUTH_OIDC_LOGIN_FAIL | outcome=failure | nis2=Y |
+  ... | claims={"sub":"mario@co.it","roles":["viewer"]}
+
