+# Patches — integration-v0.10.2
+
+**Base upstream tag:** `v0.10.2` (SHA `ecd48e2f718220a6400ecf49eafd4867a38feb10`)  
+**Regenerated:** 2026-07-02
+
+## Patch series
+
+| #    | File                                                    | Description                                                        |
+| ---- | -------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| 0001 | `chore-reconcile-fork-customizations-onto-v0.10.2-bas…`   | Full cumulative diff of all fork customizations (relative to the `v0.10.1` base) reapplied onto `v0.10.2`: NIS2 access-log/audit/OIDC compliance, analytics (TTFT/Token-s/error metrics, routing analytics, cross-filter), async save-handler fix, repo tooling docs, i18n key additions |
+| 0002 | `chore-bump-version-to-0.10.2-260701.patch`               | Version bump to `0.10.2-260701`                                    |
+
+> **Note:** this series was generated by diffing `v0.10.1..main` and applying that diff onto
+> the `v0.10.2` tag (rather than replaying the original per-feature commit history), because
+> `main` had also accumulated commits merged directly (not part of the original `integration-v0.10.1`
+> patch series documented in the previous README) between the creation and promotion of that
+> branch. Two non-textual overlaps with upstream's own `v0.10.2` changes were resolved by hand:
+> - `backend/open_webui/utils/middleware.py`: upstream added `merge_streamed_reasoning_details`
+>   at the same location as our `merge_routing_usage` helper — both kept.
+> - ~60 i18n locale JSON files: both sides added different new translation keys to the same
+>   object — both sets of keys kept.
+
+## Applying
+
+```bash
+git checkout v0.10.2
+git am patches/*.patch
+```
